---
/**
 * "Why this matters" strip — the assume-zero-knowledge hook (EWG-inspired IA).
 * A calm, CITED explanation of why sourcing is worth checking. Shared lead + close
 * frame the regulatory reality; each page passes one ingredient-specific cited
 * `example`. Every factual claim links to a resolvable primary source. Tone:
 * describe the evidence, never alarm (rulebook) — no "junk/danger" language.
 *
 * `example` is HTML (set:html) so the page can embed inline citation links.
 */
interface Props {
  example: string;
}
const { example } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="why" aria-label="Why this matters">
  <p class="eyebrow">Why this matters</p>
  <p class="body">
    Supplements are far more lightly regulated than medicines. In Australia most are
    <a href="https://www.tga.gov.au/products/medicines/listed-medicines/overview/listed-medicines" target="_blank" rel="noopener">“listed” (AUST&nbsp;L)</a>
    — the maker certifies they meet the rules and the product goes on a register, but the regulator
    doesn’t individually test what’s in each bottle before it’s sold — and products imported for
    personal use aren’t checked here at all.
  </p>
  <p class="body" set:html={example} />
  <p class="body close">
    None of this means these products are bad. It means the <strong>label is a claim, not a
    guarantee</strong> — and checking that claim is exactly what this page does.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .why {
    margin: var(--sp-6) 0;
    padding: var(--sp-5) var(--sp-6);
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    background: var(--primary-soft);
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--primary);
    margin: 0 0 var(--sp-2);
  }
  .body {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--lh-base);
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: var(--sp-3) 0 0;
    max-width: 74ch;
  }
  .body:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .close {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .why :global(a) {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
</style>
